WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:01:27.120
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
01:27.390 --> 01:34.910
[The Great Long March]

3
01:35.280 --> 01:37.810
[Episode 5]

4
01:38.570 --> 01:42.330
[Yudu River, Gannan, Jiangxi]

5
01:40.450 --> 01:41.330
Greetings, Chairman Mao.

6
01:41.330 --> 01:43.460
Thank you for your hard work, boatmen.

7
01:45.280 --> 01:46.340
This way, this way.

8
01:47.550 --> 01:48.150
Chen Geng.

9
01:48.250 --> 01:48.630
Chairman.

10
01:48.630 --> 01:49.910
Easy now. Take it slow.

11
01:50.789 --> 01:52.120
[Mao Zedong, Chairman of the Central Executive Committee and Chairman of the Council of People's Commissars of the Chinese Soviet Republic]

12
01:51.039 --> 01:52.250
So you're the head of the Cadre Regiment now?

13
01:52.250 --> 01:52.920
Yes.

14
01:52.430 --> 01:54.420
[Chen Geng, head of the Cadre Regiment of the 1st Military Commission Column]

15
01:53.789 --> 01:54.840
Reporting in, Chairman!

16
01:54.840 --> 01:55.680
I'm leading the Cadre Regiment's

17
01:55.680 --> 01:57.830
Special Engineer Company in building a pontoon bridge.

18
01:57.830 --> 01:58.780
Please give us your instructions.

19
01:58.780 --> 02:00.180
You're back on your feet?

20
02:01.560 --> 02:03.820
They seem to get better when I'm working.

21
02:04.570 --> 02:06.790
There are three outstanding men from Whampoa:

22
02:06.790 --> 02:08.530
Jiang Xianyun for his penmanship,

23
02:08.530 --> 02:09.669
He Zhonghan for his silver tongue,

24
02:09.669 --> 02:11.670
but none can match Chen Geng's legs.

25
02:11.680 --> 02:13.940
You should take better care of your legs.

26
02:14.000 --> 02:16.390
These legs of mine... It's karma.

27
02:17.240 --> 02:18.510
During the Northern Expedition,

28
02:18.510 --> 02:19.910
I saved Chiang Kai-shek.

29
02:20.310 --> 02:21.570
To save Chiang's life,

30
02:21.710 --> 02:23.970
I carried him on my back and ran for miles.

31
02:24.110 --> 02:25.840
Now I've been shot in both legs.

32
02:25.970 --> 02:27.040
That's karma.

33
02:27.690 --> 02:30.090
Generalissimo Chiang really let you down.

34
02:30.800 --> 02:31.630
If I'd known it would turn out like this,

35
02:31.630 --> 02:33.000
I should've left him by the roadside

36
02:33.000 --> 02:33.940
and let him become a martyr.

37
02:33.940 --> 02:35.430
Wouldn't that have been better than this?

38
02:35.430 --> 02:36.960
You're acting like a child.

39
02:37.240 --> 02:39.120
Even if you'd left Chiang Kai-shek to die,

40
02:39.120 --> 02:41.500
there would still be Zhang Kai-shek, Wang Kai-shek...

41
02:41.500 --> 02:43.230
It wouldn't solve the problem.

42
02:43.520 --> 02:44.650
Hearing you say that

43
02:45.100 --> 02:46.560
makes me feel much better.

44
02:47.870 --> 02:50.360
What are you doing with all those barn lanterns?

45
02:50.360 --> 02:51.960
They serve a critical purpose.

46
02:51.960 --> 02:53.260
We are building a pontoon bridge now,

47
02:53.260 --> 02:54.790
and we've run into a major problem.

48
02:54.790 --> 02:56.480
The Yudu River is too wide,

49
02:56.500 --> 02:57.850
and the current is swift.

50
02:57.850 --> 03:00.130
If we build it during the day, enemy planes will bomb us,

51
03:00.130 --> 03:01.860
so we can only build it at night.

52
03:02.440 --> 03:05.110
But the visibility is poor, and shouting can't be heard.

53
03:05.110 --> 03:07.910
The boats we're using to build the bridge keep shifting,

54
03:07.910 --> 03:09.120
which wastes time,

55
03:09.240 --> 03:11.190
and it's hard to keep the bridge aligned.

56
03:11.190 --> 03:15.590
Then Wang Yaonan, commander of the Military Commission's Engineer Battalion

57
03:15.870 --> 03:16.800
Winter boy?

58
03:16.850 --> 03:17.930
Yeah, it's him.

59
03:18.450 --> 03:21.130
He learned a method from the local people.

60
03:21.160 --> 03:22.600
The method is simple.

61
03:22.780 --> 03:24.610
It sounds very simple once you hear it.

62
03:24.610 --> 03:25.730
But if no one tells you,

63
03:25.730 --> 03:27.320
you could think forever and never come up with it.

64
03:27.320 --> 03:30.040
You put one of these lanterns

65
03:30.310 --> 03:31.760
between the bridgehead and every boat.

66
03:31.760 --> 03:34.090
When the lanterns line up, so do the boats,

67
03:34.190 --> 03:35.430
and the bridge stays straight.

68
03:35.430 --> 03:36.100
You see.

69
03:36.470 --> 03:37.430
There are wise people among ordinary folk.

70
03:37.430 --> 03:37.840
Yes.

71
03:38.070 --> 03:40.079
Even immortals come from common folks.

72
03:40.079 --> 03:42.130
Winter boy knows to seek wisdom from the people.

73
03:42.130 --> 03:42.810
Well done.

74
03:46.940 --> 03:49.500
Come on, let's get in the water.

75
03:49.880 --> 03:50.860
I'll help you build it.

76
03:50.860 --> 03:52.190
Please don't, Chairman.

77
03:52.190 --> 03:53.500
We heard you haven't been well.

78
03:53.500 --> 03:55.340
Just direct us, and we'll do the work.

79
03:55.340 --> 03:57.000
You keep calling me Chairman.

80
03:57.150 --> 03:59.510
As Chairman, I can't just sit back and do nothing.

81
03:59.510 --> 04:00.790
I need to do what I can.

82
04:01.480 --> 04:02.090
Come on.

83
04:02.120 --> 04:03.500
Chairman, you still have malaria.

84
04:03.500 --> 04:04.600
You can't go into the water.

85
04:04.600 --> 04:05.430
The last time you did,

86
04:05.430 --> 04:06.910
Director Fu Lianzhang scolded us.

87
04:06.910 --> 04:07.630
He said if you went into the river again,

88
04:07.630 --> 04:09.300
he'd make us stand at attention as punishment.

89
04:09.300 --> 04:10.050
You...

90
04:10.780 --> 04:11.620
Enough.

91
04:11.840 --> 04:14.040
You're chirping like a little sparrow.

92
05:03.070 --> 05:04.040
Runzhi.

93
05:05.970 --> 05:06.720
Qiubai.

94
05:07.410 --> 05:08.120
Runzhi.

95
05:21.860 --> 05:25.570
[Qu Qiubai, Minister of Education of the Central Executive Committee and the Council of People's Commissars of the Chinese Soviet Republic]

96
05:22.240 --> 05:25.530
Runzhi, I came specially to say goodbye.

97
05:30.310 --> 05:31.270
Qiubai.

98
05:31.360 --> 05:34.480
Through Luofu and Enlai,

99
05:35.000 --> 05:37.930
I've raised your situation with Bo Gu several times,

100
05:37.940 --> 05:40.740
but Bo Gu remained indifferent.

101
05:42.090 --> 05:43.330
I heard about it.

102
05:43.450 --> 05:45.450
I'm deeply grateful for the concern

103
05:45.659 --> 05:48.170
you and the others have shown me.

104
05:52.730 --> 05:53.800
Runzhi,

105
05:54.670 --> 05:57.110
you don't need to worry about me.

106
05:59.170 --> 06:00.770
Given the state of my health,

107
06:02.230 --> 06:04.210
I'll make peace with whatever comes.

108
06:04.210 --> 06:07.570
That day, you brought Lin Biao and Nie Rongzhen

109
06:07.850 --> 06:09.580
to visit my library.

110
06:10.240 --> 06:12.290
I asked you about the Central Committee's moves,

111
06:12.290 --> 06:13.690
but you didn't say a word.

112
06:14.240 --> 06:15.610
Still, I understood.

113
06:16.610 --> 06:18.210
You were preparing to leave.

114
06:18.520 --> 06:19.850
After thinking it over,

115
06:19.850 --> 06:21.780
I felt I had to see you one more time.

116
06:22.160 --> 06:23.490
First, to say farewell.

117
06:23.710 --> 06:26.770
Second, there are some things I must tell you in person.

118
06:27.000 --> 06:28.440
Qiubai, go ahead.

119
06:34.340 --> 06:35.390
Runzhi,

120
06:36.310 --> 06:38.000
when I first read your

121
06:38.310 --> 06:40.680
"Report on an Investigation of the Peasant Movement in Hunan"

122
06:40.680 --> 06:41.750
I knew at once

123
06:41.920 --> 06:44.310
that you, Mao Runzhi, truly understand

124
06:44.340 --> 06:46.070
China's national conditions.

125
06:47.150 --> 06:48.750
Later, I also witnessed for myself

126
06:48.750 --> 06:50.500
how you, the leader of the peasant movement,

127
06:50.500 --> 06:52.820
became a chief armed with guns in the mountains.

128
06:52.820 --> 06:55.030
You opened up a new path in Jinggang Mountain,

129
06:55.030 --> 06:57.360
and established the Central Soviet Area.

130
07:00.170 --> 07:01.770
You don't have to excuse yourself, Qiubai.

131
07:01.770 --> 07:02.720
I'm not afraid.

132
07:02.820 --> 07:04.700
I, Mao Zedong, am not that delicate.

133
07:04.700 --> 07:06.230
I know you're not afraid.

134
07:07.750 --> 07:11.160
It's because you have a longer road ahead of you than I do.

135
07:14.970 --> 07:15.970
Runzhi,

136
07:16.750 --> 07:18.410
our Party has been on this road

137
07:19.350 --> 07:21.150
for more than 13 years now.

138
07:21.660 --> 07:23.520
And we've taken many wrong turns.

139
07:23.610 --> 07:24.900
It hasn't been easy.

140
07:25.410 --> 07:27.750
Back when I was running the operations of the Central Committee,

141
07:27.750 --> 07:28.950
I also made mistakes.

142
07:29.870 --> 07:31.570
I ordered you to attack Changsha,

143
07:31.570 --> 07:33.500
but you withdrew to Jinggang Mountain instead.

144
07:33.500 --> 07:34.430
Because of that,

145
07:34.630 --> 07:36.250
I removed you from your position

146
07:36.250 --> 07:38.520
as an alternate member of the Politburo.

147
07:38.930 --> 07:42.360
And somehow, that later became a story that I had expelled you from the Party.

148
07:42.360 --> 07:43.920
But you didn't give up.

149
07:43.940 --> 07:47.350
You insisted on building rural armed bases supported by workers and peasants.

150
07:47.350 --> 07:51.390
It turns out, you were right about taking that path.

151
07:52.560 --> 07:53.710
I think

152
07:53.980 --> 07:56.610
you always see further than we do.

153
07:57.159 --> 07:57.920
Runzhi,

154
07:57.920 --> 08:00.850
the revolution is at a life-or-death turning point.

155
08:01.660 --> 08:03.590
I hope you'll be as resolute as before.

156
08:03.590 --> 08:04.740
Do not lose heart.

157
08:05.120 --> 08:08.410
When the crucial moment comes, you must step up.

158
08:10.670 --> 08:12.470
Although the current situation

159
08:12.840 --> 08:14.440
is heartbreaking.

160
08:14.460 --> 08:15.410
Qiubai.

161
08:16.960 --> 08:19.820
Speaking of heartbreaking, you and I feel the same.

162
08:20.040 --> 08:22.770
And we are not the only ones suffering.

163
08:24.360 --> 08:25.720
But pain is inevitable,

164
08:26.580 --> 08:27.980
we must never lose heart.

165
08:28.780 --> 08:30.510
Since the Fifth Counter-Encirclement Campaign,

166
08:30.510 --> 08:34.039
we've been losing ground in the Central Soviet Area, bit by bit.

167
08:34.669 --> 08:36.929
I, Mao Zedong, am heartbroken every day,

168
08:38.390 --> 08:40.450
but I haven't lost heart for a moment.

169
08:40.470 --> 08:41.740
Rest assured, Qiubai.

170
08:41.760 --> 08:43.159
We will use our own feet

171
08:43.539 --> 08:45.230
to forge a path of our own.

172
08:46.640 --> 08:48.800
Well said. Well said.

173
08:52.150 --> 08:54.910
You've lifted the biggest burden from my heart.

174
08:57.020 --> 08:59.990
Runzhi, I've said all I needed to say.

175
09:00.950 --> 09:02.420
Let's part ways here.

176
09:07.810 --> 09:08.840
Qiubai!

177
09:12.380 --> 09:14.230
We will definitely come back.

178
09:15.030 --> 09:16.060
When I come back,

179
09:16.250 --> 09:17.990
make sure you're there to welcome me home!

180
09:17.990 --> 09:19.310
Sure!

181
09:19.990 --> 09:21.110
Runzhi,

182
09:21.990 --> 09:24.370
when I came to Ruijin from Shanghai earlier this year,

183
09:24.370 --> 09:27.220
Mr. Lu Xun gave me a couplet.

184
09:27.250 --> 09:30.210
Today, I'd like to share it with you:

185
09:31.150 --> 09:34.100
A bosom friend is enough to me;

186
09:34.930 --> 09:38.410
I'll hold the same attitude to the world!

187
09:39.330 --> 09:40.210
I'm leaving.

188
10:22.060 --> 10:25.060
In the first half of October 1934,

189
10:25.890 --> 10:27.600
the main force of the Central Red Army

190
10:27.600 --> 10:29.570
set out from the assembly area in Yudu,

191
10:29.570 --> 10:32.410
Changting, Ninghua and other places,

192
10:32.840 --> 10:36.270
initiating their long march of strategic shift.

193
10:37.800 --> 10:41.080
Torches, barn lanterns, straw sandals,

194
10:41.630 --> 10:44.560
and people's reluctant, yet hopeful parting gazes,

195
10:44.980 --> 10:46.200
became the final collective memory

196
10:46.200 --> 10:48.600
of the Central Soviet Area for many Red Army

197
10:48.710 --> 10:52.110
commanders and fighters as they crossed the Yudu River.

198
10:53.020 --> 10:55.330
They did not yet know that

199
10:55.980 --> 10:58.340
this single step would take them away from their homeland,

200
10:58.340 --> 11:01.190
and many would never be able to return.

201
11:03.180 --> 11:04.980
In this final wave of farewells,

202
11:05.240 --> 11:08.330
many would never meet again.

203
11:09.680 --> 11:11.750
And this sudden turn on a heel

204
11:12.570 --> 11:14.720
would mark the end of many lives.

205
11:49.580 --> 11:52.490
[Zhou Enlai, CPC Central Committee Politburo Standing Committee, Vice-Chairman of the Central Revolutionary Military Commission, General Political Commissar of the Chinese Workers' and Peasants' Red Army]

206
11:55.370 --> 11:57.800
[Zhu Jixun, Red Army Warrior]

207
12:03.090 --> 12:04.780
[Li De, Comintern Military Advisor]

208
12:04.810 --> 12:08.680
[Bo Gu (Qin Bangxian), Head of the CPC Central Committee]

209
12:12.900 --> 12:16.460
[Luofu (Zhang Wentian), Member of the Political Bureau Standing Committee of the CPC Central Committee; Chairman of the Central Executive Committee of the Chinese Soviet Republic]

210
12:16.520 --> 12:19.410
[Wang Jiaxiang, Vice-Chairman of the Central Revolutionary Military Commission; Director of the General Political Department of the Chinese Workers' and Peasants' Red Army]

211
13:28.700 --> 13:31.630
[He Zizhen, Mao Zedong's wife]

212
13:34.590 --> 13:37.210
[Deng Yingchao, Secretary of the Political Bureau of the CPC Central Committee]

213
13:41.680 --> 13:43.240
[Kang Keqing, Zhu De's wife]

214
13:43.260 --> 13:45.540
[Liu Ying, Inspector of the Political Department of the 2nd Column of the Military Commission]

215
14:10.590 --> 14:12.440
[Dong Biwu, President of the Supreme Court of the Chinese Soviet Republic]

216
14:12.510 --> 14:15.500
[Xu Teli, Vice Minister of the Ministry of Education of the Central Executive Committee of the Chinese Soviet Republic]

217
14:56.670 --> 15:00.900
[Zhu De, Chairman of the Central Revolutionary Military Commission and Commander-in-Chief of the Chinese Workers' and Peasants' Red Army]

218
15:40.380 --> 15:41.510
Keep up. Be careful.

219
15:44.440 --> 15:45.570
Hurry up and keep up.

220
15:54.790 --> 15:55.720
Why did you stop?

221
15:58.440 --> 15:59.200
Make way.

222
16:00.480 --> 16:01.480
Stop, stop!

223
16:05.480 --> 16:07.840
Comrades, don't crowd together up ahead.

224
16:08.110 --> 16:09.240
Everyone, make way.

225
16:09.240 --> 16:12.290
Let the comrades of the field army pass first. Quickly!

226
16:12.290 --> 16:14.170
Make way, make way.

227
16:14.360 --> 16:15.560
Let us through first.

228
16:17.790 --> 16:18.950
Hurry. Hurry.

229
16:20.640 --> 16:21.560
Move.

230
16:25.440 --> 16:26.970
Take it slowly. Don't push.

231
16:27.910 --> 16:29.640
Stay in formation. Don't rush.

232
16:35.070 --> 16:35.820
Be careful.

233
16:37.870 --> 16:40.870
[Huang Zhen, Chief of the Propaganda Section of the Political Department of the Units Directly Under the Military Commission]

234
16:53.150 --> 16:55.050
Bamboo clappers ring, loud and clear.

235
16:55.050 --> 16:56.840
The Central Red Army marches far and wide.

236
16:56.840 --> 16:58.630
Crossing over mountains, we're not afraid of hardship;

237
16:58.630 --> 17:00.540
Wading through rivers, we're not afraid of trials.

238
17:00.540 --> 17:02.280
Bamboo clappers ring, look ahead.

239
17:02.280 --> 17:04.079
The road of revolution lies before us.

240
17:04.079 --> 17:05.760
Winter will pass sooner or later;

241
17:05.760 --> 17:07.609
When spring comes, the mountain flowers will bloom red.

242
17:07.609 --> 17:09.260
Comrades, work hard.

243
17:09.290 --> 17:10.440
Keep the Party's orders in mind.

244
17:10.440 --> 17:12.589
What are you doing? The ducks ran away.

245
17:13.040 --> 17:15.450
One day, victory reports will redden the sky.

246
17:15.450 --> 17:16.130
Over there.

247
17:19.260 --> 17:21.160
Bamboo clappers ring, loud and clear.

248
17:21.160 --> 17:23.109
The Central Red Army marches far and wide.

249
17:23.109 --> 17:24.920
Crossing over mountains, we're not afraid of hardship;

250
17:24.920 --> 17:26.880
Wading through rivers, we're not afraid of trials.

251
17:26.880 --> 17:28.569
Bamboo clappers ring, look ahead.

252
17:28.569 --> 17:30.440
The road of revolution lies before us.

253
17:30.440 --> 17:32.270
Winter will pass sooner or later;

254
17:32.270 --> 17:34.000
When spring comes, the mountain flowers will bloom red.

255
17:34.000 --> 17:35.590
Comrades, work hard.

256
17:35.830 --> 17:37.510
Keep the Party's orders in mind.

257
17:37.510 --> 17:39.200
Parting today is hard to bear;

258
17:38.680 --> 17:40.310
[Wu Xiuquan, Translator]

259
17:39.220 --> 17:42.660
One day, victory reports will redden the sky.

260
18:13.370 --> 18:13.670
Come on.

261
18:13.670 --> 18:14.170
Put me down.

262
18:14.170 --> 18:14.680
Come, come.

263
18:14.680 --> 18:15.610
Easy. Slow down.

264
18:21.320 --> 18:22.080
Come on.

265
18:22.300 --> 18:22.920
Help me up.

266
18:22.940 --> 18:23.860
Come on.

267
18:24.630 --> 18:25.310
Chairman.

268
18:25.530 --> 18:25.940
Let's go.

269
18:25.940 --> 18:26.860
You still have a fever.

270
18:26.860 --> 18:28.320
You need to rest on the stretcher.

271
18:28.320 --> 18:29.600
You... you can't walk.

272
18:29.960 --> 18:30.680
I'll walk.

273
18:32.830 --> 18:34.590
I've been half-conscious for two days.

274
18:34.590 --> 18:35.850
I can't sleep anymore.

275
18:37.440 --> 18:39.970
If I'm going to die, I won't die on a stretcher.

276
18:40.600 --> 18:41.360
Let's go.

277
18:57.200 --> 18:57.920
What's going on?

278
18:57.920 --> 18:59.590
Medic!

279
18:59.720 --> 19:00.240
Medic!

280
19:00.270 --> 19:01.010
Go take a look, quickly.

281
19:01.010 --> 19:01.570
Yes.

282
19:01.600 --> 19:02.760
Go help.

283
19:02.980 --> 19:05.180
Make way! Make way!

284
19:06.160 --> 19:07.380
Give us a hand. Lift him up first.

285
19:07.380 --> 19:09.250
One, two, three! Heave!

286
19:10.160 --> 19:11.920
One, two, three.

287
19:12.750 --> 19:13.880
Pull him out! Hurry!

288
19:14.070 --> 19:14.480
Move!

289
19:14.640 --> 19:15.070
Help him.

290
19:15.070 --> 19:15.550
Hurry up.

291
19:15.550 --> 19:17.110
Come on, lower it down.

292
19:21.380 --> 19:22.240
How's it going?

293
19:22.370 --> 19:23.770
Quick, take him down.

294
19:24.180 --> 19:25.380
What's in this crate?

295
19:25.880 --> 19:27.610
The hospital's X-ray machine.

296
19:27.890 --> 19:28.710
Why is it so heavy?

297
19:28.710 --> 19:29.800
It weighs several hundred kilos.

298
19:29.800 --> 19:31.060
Come on, give me a hand.

299
19:31.170 --> 19:31.550
Come on.

300
19:31.550 --> 19:32.960
Come on, lift it up.

301
19:32.980 --> 19:34.870
One, two, go, lift!

302
19:39.590 --> 19:41.210
What's in that crate they're carrying?

303
19:41.210 --> 19:42.490
The hospital's X-ray machine.

304
19:42.490 --> 19:43.730
X-ray machine?

305
19:45.720 --> 19:46.680
It's so heavy.

306
19:46.680 --> 19:48.340
It weighs a few hundred kilos.

307
19:58.490 --> 19:59.340
One, two, go!

308
19:59.440 --> 20:00.240
Go!

309
20:00.400 --> 20:02.530
One, two, go!

310
20:04.910 --> 20:05.870
The troops behind, keep up!

311
20:05.010 --> 20:06.850
[Peng Dehuai, Commander of the 3rd Red Army Corps]

312
20:07.520 --> 20:08.370
Peng.

313
20:08.390 --> 20:09.020
Mao.

314
20:09.900 --> 20:10.710
You...

315
20:11.330 --> 20:13.590
How did you get yourself into this state?

316
20:13.670 --> 20:14.630
I'm fine.

317
20:15.160 --> 20:16.160
Why are you here?

318
20:16.420 --> 20:17.680
Aren't we about to reach

319
20:17.680 --> 20:18.920
the Guangdong Army's blockade line?

320
20:18.920 --> 20:20.270
I'm going to the Military Commission to get a mission.

321
20:20.270 --> 20:21.130
What about you?

322
20:22.640 --> 20:24.260
Can you manage in your condition?

323
20:24.260 --> 20:26.370
I'm fine. I'm very well.

324
20:27.360 --> 20:30.420
Go back to your business. Military matters come first.

325
20:30.500 --> 20:31.460
Look around.

326
20:31.830 --> 20:33.270
We're moving far too slowly now.

327
20:33.270 --> 20:35.790
Look at all these pots and pans we're carrying.

328
20:35.790 --> 20:37.230
No one is willing to throw anything away.

329
20:37.230 --> 20:39.100
It's slowing down both the 1st and 3rd Red Army Corps.

330
20:39.100 --> 20:40.860
We're marching while carrying our coffins.

331
20:40.860 --> 20:42.500
Where is the mobility and flexibility

332
20:42.500 --> 20:44.560
of... of a fighting force in all this?

333
20:44.700 --> 20:45.610
Once the enemy realizes what's happening,

334
20:45.610 --> 20:47.440
take an air raid, for example.

335
20:47.820 --> 20:48.940
Look at our troops, they won't even

336
20:48.940 --> 20:50.400
find a place to take cover!

337
20:59.260 --> 21:03.170
Mao, take care.

338
21:06.480 --> 21:07.330
Peng.

339
21:14.950 --> 21:17.320
Take this.

340
21:17.620 --> 21:19.840
You can read it when you stop for the night.

341
21:19.840 --> 21:21.900
Perfect. The book you gave me before,

342
21:22.330 --> 21:25.020
"Two Tactics of Social-Democracy in the Democratic Revolution,"

343
21:25.020 --> 21:26.480
I've finished reading it.

344
21:26.960 --> 21:29.560
I'll definitely read this one carefully, too.

345
21:32.170 --> 21:32.900
I'm leaving.

346
21:44.090 --> 21:44.960
Runzhi.

347
21:50.080 --> 21:51.430
Is that you?

348
21:52.570 --> 21:54.290
Mr. Dong, it's me.

349
21:54.880 --> 21:56.960
Are you really Runzhi? You...

350
21:57.120 --> 21:58.080
Mr. Xu.

351
21:58.370 --> 22:00.930
Runzhi, what happened to you?

352
22:02.510 --> 22:04.600
The high-spirited disease.

353
22:04.930 --> 22:07.410
You've got malaria? Can you handle it?

354
22:06.310 --> 22:07.320
[Xie Juezai, Secretary-General of the Central Government of the Chinese Soviet Republic]

355
22:07.590 --> 22:08.910
I'm fine.

356
22:09.750 --> 22:12.550
Thank you for your hard work, gentlemen.

357
22:14.270 --> 22:16.340
Runzhi, you're terribly ill.

358
22:16.790 --> 22:18.050
You should be resting.

359
22:18.110 --> 22:19.570
Why are you still reading?

360
22:19.820 --> 22:22.290
One never stops learning, sir.

361
22:23.140 --> 22:24.900
Runzhi, with malaria like this,

362
22:24.570 --> 22:28.390
Lin Boqu, Minister of Finance of the Central Government of the Chinese Soviet Republic]

363
22:25.130 --> 22:27.640
you must get back on the stretcher,

364
22:27.700 --> 22:28.880
cover yourself with a blanket,

365
22:28.880 --> 22:30.520
and sweat it out.

366
22:30.640 --> 22:31.350
That's right.

367
22:31.350 --> 22:33.640
Mr. Lin, lying on a stretcher isn't

368
22:34.000 --> 22:35.670
necessarily the only way to fight malaria.

369
22:35.670 --> 22:37.800
I'm thinking of a way to deal with it.

370
22:38.680 --> 22:41.340
Just as the author of this book Engels once said,

371
22:42.050 --> 22:44.640
Marx's entire worldview

372
22:44.860 --> 22:46.170
is not a doctrine,

373
22:46.930 --> 22:48.260
but a method.

374
22:48.570 --> 22:50.900
What he provides is not ready-made dogma,

375
22:51.100 --> 22:53.430
but a starting point for further research

376
22:54.180 --> 22:56.700
and a method for conducting that research.

377
22:59.190 --> 23:01.040
Runzhi is trying to prove

378
23:01.310 --> 23:04.640
that Marxism can take root even in these mountain valleys.

379
23:08.020 --> 23:09.060
Runzhi,

380
23:09.210 --> 23:11.490
where are we headed?

381
23:16.110 --> 23:19.990
For now, we need to break through the encirclement.

382
23:21.920 --> 23:22.390
Let's go.

383
23:22.390 --> 23:23.110
Let's go.

384
23:23.140 --> 23:24.230
Take care.

385
23:36.310 --> 23:38.830
Chairman, please lie on the stretcher.

386
23:46.890 --> 23:48.260
I can't walk anymore.

387
23:48.340 --> 23:50.450
Gou, get up.

388
23:51.310 --> 23:53.270
You're disobeying orders, aren't you?

389
23:53.270 --> 23:54.880
Look at these people in the Red Army.

390
23:54.880 --> 23:56.680
Who would dare disobey an order?

391
23:57.160 --> 23:59.010
If you won't obey, go home.

392
24:05.000 --> 24:07.960
You want to avenge your father like this?

393
24:08.240 --> 24:10.500
Then go home and avenge him from your bed!

394
24:21.470 --> 24:22.870
I promised my mother that

395
24:23.120 --> 24:25.120
I'd stay with the Red Army to the end.

396
24:25.800 --> 24:27.540
One day, I'll join a combat unit.

397
24:27.540 --> 24:30.540
You're really stubborn, kid.

398
24:31.510 --> 24:32.840
You're just like my son.

399
24:33.000 --> 24:34.860
I got you assigned to the mess unit

400
24:35.070 --> 24:36.680
because you look like my son.

401
24:37.310 --> 24:38.840
If your ears stuck out more,

402
24:39.400 --> 24:41.060
you'd look even more like him.

403
24:41.930 --> 24:43.930
You keep saying I look like your son.

404
24:44.550 --> 24:46.160
Is he in the Red Army too?

405
24:47.310 --> 24:48.440
Where is your son?

406
24:50.130 --> 24:51.500
How old is he?

407
24:53.110 --> 24:54.520
Get on with your march.

408
24:55.100 --> 24:56.710
You sure talk a lot.

409
25:04.920 --> 25:06.310
Just as the Central Red Army

410
25:06.310 --> 25:08.680
began its strategic shift,

411
25:09.240 --> 25:11.440
the 6th Red Army Corps, which had moved west in advance,

412
25:11.440 --> 25:14.030
was intercepted by KMT troops

413
25:14.050 --> 25:16.880
in the Ganxi area of Shiqian County, Guizhou Province.

414
25:16.880 --> 25:19.080
The corps were split into three groups.

415
25:19.590 --> 25:22.310
Chief of Staff Li Da led part of the advance force

416
25:22.310 --> 25:23.830
and some soldiers from the machine-gun company,

417
25:23.830 --> 25:25.030
more than 400 men in all;

418
25:25.030 --> 25:27.750
Including the 50th Red Regiment covered the main force's retreat,

419
25:27.750 --> 25:30.030
they all lost contact with the main force.

420
25:30.030 --> 25:32.430
Ren Bishi, Xiao Ke, and Wang Zhen

421
25:32.680 --> 25:34.720
led the main force of the corps southward

422
25:34.720 --> 25:36.650
into the remote mountain forests.

423
25:36.960 --> 25:37.590
Soon after,

424
25:37.590 --> 25:40.630
when the main force advanced toward Ganxi again, Long Yun,

425
25:40.630 --> 25:44.430
commander of the 18th Red Division, was captured while badly wounded,

426
25:44.430 --> 25:46.760
and later killed by the enemy in Changsha.

427
25:47.490 --> 25:50.790
Many Red Army soldiers who covered the main force's retreat at Kunniu Mountain

428
25:50.790 --> 25:53.520
jumped off the cliff and sacrificed themselves.

429
25:54.690 --> 25:55.720
On October 15,

430
25:56.050 --> 25:59.500
Li Da and others unexpectedly encountered the 3rd Red Army

431
25:59.520 --> 26:01.850
at Fengxiangxi in Yanhe County, Guizhou.

432
26:02.010 --> 26:04.520
After learning what had happened, He Long, commander of the 3rd Red Army,

433
26:04.520 --> 26:05.750
and Political Commissar Guan Xiangying

434
26:05.750 --> 26:08.790
immediately led the main force of the 3rd Red Army southward.

435
26:08.790 --> 26:10.640
On the morning of October 24th,

436
26:10.750 --> 26:13.510
at Sanjia Village in Muhuang Town, Yinjiang County,

437
26:13.510 --> 26:16.510
they successfully reunited with the main force of the 6th Red Army Corps.

438
26:15.080 --> 26:18.900
[Sanjia Village, Muhuang Town, Yinjiang County, Guizhou]

439
26:19.480 --> 26:21.440
The 6th Red Army Corps is here!

440
26:21.830 --> 26:24.270
The 6th Red Army Corps is here!

441
26:24.850 --> 26:27.050
The 6th Red Army Corps is here!

442
27:04.900 --> 27:06.360
The rendezvous at Muhuang

443
27:06.480 --> 27:10.060
was the first time Red Army forces joined up during the strategic shift.

444
27:10.060 --> 27:13.340
It marked the success of the 6th Red Army Corps' westward expedition

445
27:13.340 --> 27:15.510
and paved the way for

446
27:15.540 --> 27:17.930
the Central Red Army's strategic shift.

447
27:18.520 --> 27:21.450
The rendezvous created a new strategic strike force

448
27:22.040 --> 27:24.480
and laid the foundation for the later formation

449
27:24.480 --> 27:26.480
of the 2nd Front Army of the Red Army.

450
27:27.210 --> 27:28.820
After the rendezvous at Muhuang

451
27:28.820 --> 27:30.310
under orders from the Central Committee,

452
27:30.310 --> 27:33.590
the 3rd Red Army resumed the designation of the 2nd Red Army Corps.

453
27:33.280 --> 27:35.400
[Rudolf Alfred Bosshardt, Missionary]

454
27:33.880 --> 27:35.810
He Long served as Corps Commander,

455
27:36.030 --> 27:38.400
Ren Bishi as Political Commissar,

456
27:38.560 --> 27:40.960
Guan Xiangying as the Deputy Political Commissar,

457
27:40.960 --> 27:42.830
Li Da as Chief of Staff,

458
27:43.090 --> 27:45.890
and Zhang Ziyi as the director of the Political Department.

459
27:45.890 --> 27:47.180
Xiao Ke continued to serve

460
27:47.180 --> 27:49.700
as Corps Commander of the 6th Red Army Corps,

461
27:49.790 --> 27:51.960
while Wang Zhen remained as Political Commissar.

462
27:51.960 --> 27:53.810
Tan Jiashu as Chief of Staff,

463
27:54.550 --> 27:57.440
and Gan Siqi as director of the Political Department.

464
27:57.440 --> 28:01.110
[Ren Bishi, Member of the Political Bureau of the CPC Central Committee; Political Commissar of the 2nd Red Army Corps]

465
27:57.570 --> 28:01.430
I owe Comrade He Long an apology.

466
28:02.120 --> 28:02.800
Apology?

467
28:03.440 --> 28:04.100
[Wang Zhen, Political Commissar of the 6th Red Army Corps]

468
28:03.920 --> 28:04.960
A few days ago,

469
28:04.980 --> 28:07.210
we were wandering through the mountains.

470
28:07.210 --> 28:10.690
We had no choice but to mention your name, Commander He.

471
28:10.580 --> 28:13.850
[He Long, Commander of the 2nd Red Army Corps]

472
28:11.700 --> 28:12.960
When the locals along the way heard

473
28:12.960 --> 28:14.080
we were He Long's troops,

474
28:14.080 --> 28:15.360
they gave us food and

475
28:15.380 --> 28:16.880
provided guides whenever we needed them.

476
28:16.880 --> 28:18.790
They guided us all the way

477
28:18.810 --> 28:20.270
out of the deep mountains.

478
28:20.510 --> 28:21.720
That's a good thing.

479
28:22.030 --> 28:23.860
Why are you apologizing?

480
28:23.980 --> 28:25.980
We're all one family in the Red Army.

481
28:26.510 --> 28:28.560
After we came out of the deep mountains,

482
28:28.560 --> 28:29.850
the enemy simply didn't believe it.

483
28:29.850 --> 28:30.990
Later, the rumors grew more and more far-fetched,

484
28:29.950 --> 28:32.890
[Xiao Ke, Commander of the 6th Red Army Corps]

485
28:31.000 --> 28:33.660
saying that we were guided by the mountain gods.

486
28:34.790 --> 28:36.100
There are no mountain gods.

487
28:36.100 --> 28:36.820
I think it's the people

488
28:36.820 --> 28:38.820
who are the real mountain gods.

489
28:39.100 --> 28:40.210
Well said.

490
28:40.640 --> 28:41.720
Comrade Bishi,

491
28:41.930 --> 28:44.600
you're a member of the Central Committee's Political Bureau.

492
28:44.600 --> 28:45.910
I'd like to report

493
28:46.090 --> 28:48.090
on the situation in the 3rd Red Army.

494
28:49.180 --> 28:49.900
Okay.

495
28:50.320 --> 28:52.380
After the Nanchang Uprising failed,

496
28:52.600 --> 28:55.930
the Central Committee wanted to send me to the Soviet Union.

497
28:56.180 --> 28:57.640
But I didn't make it there.

498
28:57.960 --> 28:59.240
I went from Shanghai

499
28:59.350 --> 29:00.480
back to Xiangxi.

500
29:00.880 --> 29:02.140
After several ups and downs,

501
29:02.140 --> 29:03.740
the 2nd Red Corps was formed.

502
29:04.330 --> 29:05.400
At our peak,

503
29:05.640 --> 29:08.090
we had 20,000 to 30,000 troops.

504
29:09.070 --> 29:10.660
In October 1930,

505
29:11.010 --> 29:12.980
we received orders from the Central Committee

506
29:12.980 --> 29:15.010
to cross the Yangtze River and move south,

507
29:15.010 --> 29:18.210
and cooperate with the 1st Front Army to attack Changsha.

508
29:18.510 --> 29:20.480
Later, we suffered heavy losses.

509
29:20.750 --> 29:22.720
Only a little over 3,000 troops were left.

510
29:22.720 --> 29:24.110
The Central Committee ordered us

511
29:24.110 --> 29:26.200
to abolish the designation of the 2nd Red Corps

512
29:26.200 --> 29:28.330
and redesignate it as the 3rd Red Army.

513
29:28.960 --> 29:31.020
Later, after reaching the base area,

514
29:31.020 --> 29:32.150
we continued to grow

515
29:32.270 --> 29:35.510
and expanded to more than 14,000 troops.

516
29:35.710 --> 29:36.750
But at that time,

517
29:36.920 --> 29:38.890
the Central Committee sent Comrade Xia Xi to us.

518
29:38.890 --> 29:40.010
As soon as he arrived,

519
29:40.010 --> 29:41.480
he launched political purges.

520
29:41.480 --> 29:43.690
In the end, we were left with just over 3,000 men.

521
29:43.690 --> 29:45.440
There were very few Party members left.

522
29:45.440 --> 29:47.820
We had to leave the Xiang-E-Xi base area

523
29:47.850 --> 29:49.050
and move to Qiandong.

524
29:50.820 --> 29:52.410
After arriving in Qiandong,

525
29:52.410 --> 29:55.010
we spent several months expanding the Red Army

526
29:55.640 --> 29:57.200
and made some progress.

527
29:57.260 --> 29:58.660
Now we have 4,000 people.

528
29:58.660 --> 30:01.330
We also took in 1,000 Divine Soldiers.

529
30:01.880 --> 30:02.880
Divine Soldiers?

530
30:02.910 --> 30:04.170
These Divine Soldiers

531
30:04.170 --> 30:07.170
are local armed groups in Qiandong.

532
30:07.620 --> 30:08.630
For years, they've been

533
30:08.630 --> 30:11.160
fighting against the reactionary warlords.

534
30:11.240 --> 30:12.850
They are all poor people,

535
30:13.110 --> 30:16.040
and their organization still has some feudal elements.

536
30:16.040 --> 30:18.510
ut after we educated them and reformed their organization,

537
30:18.510 --> 30:19.850
they've made rapid progress.

538
30:19.850 --> 30:21.960
[Zhang Ziyi, Director of the Political Department of the 2nd Red Army Corps; Guan Xiangying, Deputy Political Commissar of the 2nd Red Army Corps]

539
30:20.550 --> 30:22.480
Commander He, your ability to raise troops

540
30:22.480 --> 30:24.850
is renowned throughout the Party.

541
30:25.990 --> 30:26.710
Not at all.

542
30:26.990 --> 30:28.450
It's not that I'm capable.

543
30:28.590 --> 30:30.590
It's mainly because the people here

544
30:30.710 --> 30:31.910
have suffered so much.

545
30:31.910 --> 30:33.240
They need a revolution.

546
30:34.640 --> 30:35.570
Comrade He Long,

547
30:36.160 --> 30:39.510
now that we have joined forces,

548
30:40.130 --> 30:41.660
what is your plan?

549
30:47.750 --> 30:48.830
My plan

550
30:49.090 --> 30:51.400
is that the Party can't go on like this.

551
30:51.810 --> 30:53.880
We must stand united

552
30:54.200 --> 30:55.920
and make a breakthrough.

553
30:59.060 --> 31:02.460
The Central Committee is now carrying out a strategic shift,

554
31:02.770 --> 31:05.500
and doesn't have a full picture of our situation.

555
31:05.520 --> 31:07.720
A recent telegram from the Central Revolutionary Military Commission ordered us

556
31:07.720 --> 31:10.620
to have the 6th Red Army Corps and the 2nd Red Army Corps operate separately.

557
31:10.620 --> 31:12.100
They want the 6th Red Army Corps

558
31:12.100 --> 31:14.340
to advance alone into western Hunan,

559
31:14.640 --> 31:17.310
develop guerrilla warfare and establish a new Soviet area.

560
31:17.310 --> 31:19.720
The 6th Red Army Corps now has just over 3,000 troops.

561
31:19.720 --> 31:21.610
We've just fought our way out of an encirclement.

562
31:21.610 --> 31:23.070
The troops are exhausted,

563
31:23.110 --> 31:24.900
and we're short of weapons and ammunition.

564
31:24.900 --> 31:25.790
At a time like this,

565
31:25.790 --> 31:27.390
it it will be difficult for us

566
31:27.440 --> 31:29.170
to establish a base in Xiangxi.

567
31:30.850 --> 31:32.860
The 2nd Red Army Corps is in the similar situation.

568
31:32.860 --> 31:34.440
We have just over 4,000 troops.

569
31:34.440 --> 31:36.050
The enemy is sending

570
31:36.080 --> 31:37.450
more and more "encirclement" forces

571
31:37.450 --> 31:38.620
into Qiandong.

572
31:38.680 --> 31:41.120
It'll also be difficult for us to hold our ground here.

573
31:41.120 --> 31:43.180
Our two corps have finally joined up.

574
31:43.680 --> 31:46.110
If two poor brothers stand together,

575
31:46.360 --> 31:49.120
we might build a base of our own.

576
31:49.790 --> 31:52.420
But now we're supposed to split up

577
31:52.850 --> 31:53.920
and fend for ourselves separately.

578
31:53.920 --> 31:56.440
Isn't this giving the enemy an opportunity?

579
31:57.380 --> 31:59.580
Comrade He Long, tell us what you think.

580
32:03.700 --> 32:05.170
My view is

581
32:06.870 --> 32:08.270
that we must not split up.

582
32:08.500 --> 32:10.630
Our two corps should operate together

583
32:10.900 --> 32:12.660
and go to the upper reaches of the Lishui River.

584
32:12.660 --> 32:14.390
That was where our old base was.

585
32:14.410 --> 32:15.920
The people there support us,

586
32:15.920 --> 32:17.650
and the terrain is in our favor.

587
32:17.830 --> 32:20.720
In Yongshun, Longshan, Dayong,

588
32:20.880 --> 32:22.880
and Sangzhi, we can mobilize the people

589
32:22.880 --> 32:24.480
and establish our own base area.

590
32:24.480 --> 32:27.030
That way, we can still draw in

591
32:27.270 --> 32:29.440
the KMT troops from Hunan and Hubei

592
32:29.520 --> 32:32.520
to support the Central Committee's strategic shift.

593
32:40.290 --> 32:44.530
Can we win and hold our ground?

594
32:45.330 --> 32:46.730
One corps couldn't do it,

595
32:46.730 --> 32:49.010
but two corps certainly can.

596
32:49.520 --> 32:52.320
But I'm afraid the Central Committee won't agree.

597
32:55.330 --> 32:56.240
Then we should

598
32:56.360 --> 32:58.150
send a telegram to the Central Committee

599
32:58.150 --> 32:59.990
in the name of the 2nd and 6th Red Army Corps

600
32:59.990 --> 33:01.650
and put forward our proposal.

601
33:04.400 --> 33:05.540
Great.

602
33:09.300 --> 33:12.830
[Xinfeng, Ganzhou, Jiangxi; The frontline of the Guangdong Army's blockade line]

603
33:10.110 --> 33:13.020
On the night of October 21, 1934,

604
33:13.710 --> 33:15.790
under orders from the Central Revolutionary Military Commission,

605
33:15.790 --> 33:17.680
the main forces of the Central Red Army

606
33:17.680 --> 33:19.830
launched attacks from Wangmudu, Hanfang,

607
33:19.830 --> 33:21.460
Jinji, and Xintian

608
33:21.590 --> 33:24.150
against the first blockade line

609
33:24.260 --> 33:25.570
held by the Guangdong Army.

610
33:25.420 --> 33:26.510
[Hong Chao, Division Commander of the 3rd Red Army Corps]

611
33:40.140 --> 33:41.570
The Communist army is coming!

612
33:41.570 --> 33:43.280
The Communist army is coming!

613
33:44.880 --> 33:45.510
Fire!

614
34:00.350 --> 34:02.700
Comrades, charge!

615
34:32.199 --> 34:32.909
Bo Gu,

616
34:33.239 --> 34:35.590
we must take this place as soon as possible.

617
34:33.330 --> 34:36.969
[Anyuan County, Ganzhou, Jiangxi; Temporary command post of the Central Revolutionary Military Commission]

618
34:36.659 --> 34:37.360
Why haven't we

619
34:37.360 --> 34:38.230
taken this place yet?

620
34:38.230 --> 34:38.920
Commander.

621
34:39.469 --> 34:40.550
The Guangdong Army shows no sign

622
34:40.550 --> 34:42.320
of withdrawing from its defensive line.

623
34:42.320 --> 34:43.760
Due to the lack of heavy weapons,

624
34:43.760 --> 34:44.960
we have suffered heavy casualties.

625
34:44.960 --> 34:47.750
Comrade Hong Chao, Commander of the 4th Division of the 3rd Red Army Corps,

626
34:47.750 --> 34:48.480
has been killed.

627
34:48.480 --> 34:50.960
Comrade Hong Chao has been killed.

628
34:57.770 --> 34:58.690
Comrade Enlai,

629
34:58.730 --> 35:00.290
didn't you notify

630
35:00.480 --> 35:02.030
Chen Jitang's side

631
35:02.030 --> 35:03.150
of our marching route in advance?

632
35:03.150 --> 35:05.110
Why didn't they follow the previous agreement

633
35:05.110 --> 35:06.370
and let us pass through the defense line?

634
35:06.370 --> 35:08.370
I said it before.

635
35:09.000 --> 35:11.880
Warlords cannot be trusted.

636
35:12.040 --> 35:14.730
They have no integrity.

637
35:15.070 --> 35:17.130
It takes time to contact Chen Jitang.

638
35:17.350 --> 35:18.320
We left in a hurry,

639
35:18.320 --> 35:19.920
and everything was highly confidential.

640
35:19.920 --> 35:22.280
Even our own troops didn't know the details.

641
35:22.280 --> 35:25.370
I'm afraid the Guangdong Army's likely to respond even more slowly.

642
35:25.370 --> 35:26.230
Comrade Enlai,

643
35:26.420 --> 35:27.520
you still need to send someone

644
35:27.520 --> 35:29.320
to contact Chen Jitang's people urgently,

645
35:29.320 --> 35:31.780
and negotiate with them as soon as possible.

646
35:33.670 --> 35:34.460
Okay.

647
35:36.620 --> 35:37.480
Comrade Zhu De.

648
35:39.020 --> 35:40.750
I was just studying this route.

649
36:05.370 --> 36:07.760
[Huang Kecheng, Political Commissar of the 4th Division of the 3rd Red Army Corps]

650
37:08.750 --> 37:11.580
[Yang Shangkun, Political Commissar of the 3rd Red Army Corps]

651
37:32.360 --> 37:34.060
[Deng Ping, Chief of Staff of 3rd Red Army Corps]

652
37:40.820 --> 37:42.950
You are the second division commander

653
37:44.410 --> 37:46.260
our 4th Red Division has lost

654
37:48.130 --> 37:50.290
in less than a year.

655
39:05.550 --> 39:08.480
On October 25, 1934,

656
39:09.030 --> 39:13.090
the 1st and 2nd Columns of the Military Commission crossed the Tao River.

657
39:13.580 --> 39:14.770
The Central Red Army,

658
39:14.770 --> 39:17.560
at the cost of over 3,700 casualties,

659
39:17.730 --> 39:20.250
broke through the first blockade line

660
39:20.400 --> 39:22.400
set by the KMT troops.

661
39:25.410 --> 39:29.100
[Guangdong, Guangzhou, Chen Jitang's Residence]

662
39:26.000 --> 39:27.120
It's strange.

663
39:28.010 --> 39:29.030
Since the Communist army

664
39:29.030 --> 39:31.030
finished negotiating with us at Luotang a few days ago,

665
39:31.030 --> 39:33.090
there hasn't been any news from them.

666
39:33.360 --> 39:34.850
Are they moving or not?

667
39:35.140 --> 39:36.400
The "Iron Bucket Plan"

668
39:36.410 --> 39:37.800
is about to be put into action.

669
39:37.800 --> 39:41.090
[Yu Hanmou, Commander of the 1st Army of the Guangdong Army]

670
39:38.170 --> 39:39.500
If they don't move soon,

671
39:40.160 --> 39:41.590
they will be in real danger.

672
39:41.240 --> 39:44.200
[Chen Jitang, Commander-in-Chief of the Southern Route Army; Commander-in-Chief of the Guangdong Army]

673
39:49.110 --> 39:50.840
Report, Commander-in-Chief.

674
39:50.960 --> 39:54.320
We've just received an urgent notice from the Communist army.

675
39:54.320 --> 39:55.760
They have begun their transfer

676
39:55.640 --> 39:59.250
[Yang Youmin, Major General Counselor of the Guangdong Army Headquarters]

677
39:55.900 --> 39:59.630
and are asking us to let them pass under our previous agreement.

678
40:00.370 --> 40:01.970
The Communist army has left?

679
40:02.360 --> 40:02.960
Yes.

680
40:03.010 --> 40:04.210
How come I, the commander-in-chief of this defense area,

681
40:04.210 --> 40:05.670
haven't heard a word about it?

682
40:05.670 --> 40:07.370
They must have moved out suddenly during the night.

683
40:07.370 --> 40:08.710
What exactly did they say?

684
40:08.710 --> 40:09.320
They stated

685
40:09.320 --> 40:12.260
that they would pass through Wangmudu, Xintian, and otehr areas,

686
40:12.260 --> 40:14.400
and cross the Tao River as they moved west.

687
40:14.400 --> 40:16.500
They claimed they were simply passing through on their way west,

688
40:16.500 --> 40:18.360
and promised not to enter the interior of Guangdong.

689
40:18.360 --> 40:19.180
Can they be trusted?

690
40:19.180 --> 40:22.510
So far, we haven't found any evidence that they're planning anything else.

691
40:22.510 --> 40:24.440
Report! An urgent dispatch from the front!

692
40:24.440 --> 40:24.920
Read it!

693
40:25.250 --> 40:27.390
Last night, the Communist army suddenly launched attacks on Wangmudu, Hanfang,

694
40:27.390 --> 40:28.910
Jinji, and Xintian.

695
40:29.080 --> 40:30.820
Several of our defensive lines were breached,

696
40:30.820 --> 40:32.480
and we suffered heavy losses.

697
40:39.850 --> 40:40.660
See?

698
40:41.530 --> 40:43.980
They attacked without warning. They have no integrity at all!

699
40:43.980 --> 40:45.180
Since we had an agreement,

700
40:45.180 --> 40:47.480
they should at least have let us know, even if they were in a hurry.

701
40:47.480 --> 40:50.360
The Communist army's actions are certainly hard to justify.

702
40:50.360 --> 40:52.420
But the situation is urgent right now.

703
40:52.420 --> 40:53.710
If we keep fighting,

704
40:53.860 --> 40:57.450
we may have no choice but to let them through.

705
40:57.720 --> 40:58.980
Commander-in-Chief.

706
41:02.610 --> 41:03.870
Commander-in-Chief?

707
41:05.170 --> 41:06.100
Issue the order:

708
41:07.070 --> 41:08.590
all our main forces are to withdraw

709
41:08.590 --> 41:12.120
and assemble in the areas around Anyuan, Xinfeng, and Nankang.

710
41:12.280 --> 41:13.940
Clear a route for the Red Army.

711
41:14.280 --> 41:17.880
Commander, aren't you afraid the Generalissimo will blame you?

712
41:18.120 --> 41:20.080
Do you think Chiang will trust me

713
41:20.110 --> 41:22.240
if I refuse to make way for the Red Army?

714
41:23.290 --> 41:24.690
The grudge from the split

715
41:24.840 --> 41:26.360
between Nanjing and Guangdong in 1931—

716
41:26.360 --> 41:29.120
he will never forget it, not in his wildest dreams.

717
41:29.120 --> 41:30.520
What troubles me most right now

718
41:30.520 --> 41:32.320
is that I can neither lose

719
41:32.600 --> 41:33.850
nor win this battle.

720
41:34.640 --> 41:37.450
If I lose, the Communist army will enter Guangdong,

721
41:37.450 --> 41:38.740
and Chiang will say,

722
41:38.900 --> 41:40.850
"I'll help you suppress the Communists."

723
41:40.850 --> 41:42.770
Then he'll take control of Guangdong.

724
41:42.770 --> 41:43.770
If we win,

725
41:44.210 --> 41:45.460
the Communist army will be wiped out,

726
41:45.460 --> 41:47.970
but the Guangdong Army will suffer heavy losses as well.

727
41:47.970 --> 41:49.490
Then Chiang will say,

728
41:49.840 --> 41:51.840
"I'll come clean up the mess for you."

729
41:51.840 --> 41:54.640
And he'd still end up taking control of Guangdong.

730
41:54.940 --> 41:57.340
So what's your plan, Commander-in-Chief?

731
41:58.100 --> 41:59.750
A while ago, Bai Chongxi

732
41:59.900 --> 42:01.660
came to see me in Junmenling,

733
42:01.690 --> 42:03.160
and gave me an idea.

734
42:04.030 --> 42:05.120
Bai Chongxi said that

735
42:05.120 --> 42:07.230
when facing the Red Army, we can adopt this strategy:

736
42:07.230 --> 42:11.790
don't hit the head, don't cut the waist, just strike the tail.

737
42:11.980 --> 42:14.160
See the guests off and let them pass quickly.

738
42:14.160 --> 42:15.370
What do you two think?

739
42:16.240 --> 42:18.370
That's an excellent idea, Commander.

740
42:23.270 --> 42:27.210
[Rucheng, Hunan; Red Army Temporary Station]

741
42:41.200 --> 42:43.060
Hurry up. They'll be hungry soon.

742
42:43.320 --> 42:43.800
Okay.

743
42:52.970 --> 42:53.700
Guo.

744
42:54.500 --> 42:55.350
Guo!

745
42:55.750 --> 42:56.700
What's for lunch today?

746
42:56.700 --> 42:57.680
We're... we're having steamed cornbread.

747
42:57.680 --> 42:59.750
Hurry up. I'm so starving that my stomach hurts.

748
42:59.750 --> 43:00.580
Okay, okay.
